\newlabel{fig:daif-erp-predictions}{{3}{1}{Distributional prediction error predicts graded N400/P600 amplitudes across all eight case roles. \textbf {Left}: simulated ERP waveforms for three violation conditions---congruent (NOM→NOM), mild (ACC→NOM), and strong (VOC→NOM)---showing component timing and amplitude scaling per \autoref {eq:eq-7c-n400}--\autoref {eq:eq-7c-p600}. \textbf {Middle}: scatter of enriched weight \(\pi {}\) versus distributional prediction error (DPE, \autoref {eq:eq-7c-dpe}) for all roles, with regression line and \(R^2\). \textbf {Right}: predicted versus literature-typical N400/P600 amplitudes. VOC→NOM (weight \(\approx 0\)) elicits the largest P600; GEN→ACC (moderate weight) elicits a pronounced N400 but attenuated P600. Generated programmatically from \protect \texttt {src.visualization.daif\_plots.plot\_erp\_predictions()} (amplitudes from \protect \texttt {erp\_amplitude\_profile()} and related APIs in \protect \texttt {src/daif/prediction.py})}{fig:daif-erp-predictions}{}}
\@writefile{snm}{\beamer@slide {fig:daif-erp-predictions}{1}}
